1
00:05:18,947 --> 00:05:24,947
The perfect love story. Until it became the perfect crime.

2
00:10:37,894 --> 00:10:43,894
All Good Things is a mystery, thriller, romance film directed by Andrew Jarecki.

3
00:15:56,842 --> 00:16:02,842
Newly-discovered facts, court records and speculation are used to elaborate the true love story
and murder mystery of the most notorious unsolved murder case in New York history.

4
00:21:15,789 --> 00:21:21,789
David Marks, played by Ryan Gosling.

5
00:26:34,736 --> 00:26:40,736
Katie Marks, played by Kirsten Dunst.

6
00:31:53,684 --> 00:31:59,684
Sanford Marks, played by Frank Langella.

7
00:37:12,631 --> 00:37:18,631
Deborah Lehrman, played by Lily Rabe.

8
00:42:31,578 --> 00:42:37,578
Malvern Bump, played by Philip Baker Hall.

9
00:47:50,526 --> 00:47:56,526
Daniel Marks, played by Michael Esper.

10
00:53:09,473 --> 00:53:15,473
All Good Things is a 2010 American mystery/crime romantic drama film directed by
Andrew Jarecki and written by Marcus Hinchey and Marc Smerling.

11
00:58:28,421 --> 00:58:34,421
Inspired by the life of Robert Durst, it stars Ryan
Gosling, Kirsten Dunst, and Frank Langella.

12
01:03:47,368 --> 01:03:53,368
Gosling portrays the wealthy son of a New York real estate tycoon (Langella) who develops a disturbing relationship with
his wife (Dunst) and becomes suspected of a series of murders, as well as his wife's unsolved disappearance.

13
01:09:06,315 --> 01:09:12,315
All Good Things was filmed between April and July
2008 in Connecticut and New York.

14
01:14:25,263 --> 01:14:31,263
Originally scheduled for a July 24, 2009 release, the film
ultimately received a limited release on December 3, 2010.

15
01:19:44,210 --> 01:19:50,210
Durst professed admiration for the film, and after previously not
cooperating with journalists, offered to be interviewed by Jarecki.

16
01:25:03,157 --> 01:25:09,157
Durst would ultimately sit with Jarecki for more than 20 hours over a multi-year
period, which led to the true crime documentary series The Jinx in 2015.

17
01:30:22,105 --> 01:30:28,105
The film explores themes of difficult childhood, patriarch,
childhood trauma, dysfunctional marriage.

18
01:35:41,052 --> 01:35:47,052
The tone is intense and lighthearted and emotional.
